1
00:00:03,399 --> 00:00:04,793
Ladies and gentlemen,

2
00:00:04,793 --> 00:00:06,519
welcome to the main event.

3
00:00:06,779 --> 00:00:07,926
In the left corner,

4
00:00:07,926 --> 00:00:10,279
going after the smallest balance first:

5
00:00:10,279 --> 00:00:11,366
the Debt Snowball!

6
00:00:11,626 --> 00:00:13,006
And in the right corner,

7
00:00:13,006 --> 00:00:15,192
going after the highest interest rate:

8
00:00:15,192 --> 00:00:16,285
the Debt Avalanche!

9
00:00:16,545 --> 00:00:18,589
Two proven ways to crush debt.

10
00:00:18,589 --> 00:00:20,019
One saves more money.

11
00:00:20,019 --> 00:00:22,063
The other keeps you motivated.

12
00:00:22,063 --> 00:00:22,676
Who wins?

13
00:00:22,676 --> 00:00:24,175
Let's run the numbers.

14
00:00:25,575 --> 00:00:27,514
Welcome back to Broke to Balance.

15
00:00:27,774 --> 00:00:28,528
Quick note:

16
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,899
this is educational,

17
00:00:29,899 --> 00:00:31,955
not personal financial advice.

18
00:00:31,955 --> 00:00:34,629
And no payoff method works if you can't

19
00:00:34,629 --> 00:00:36,548
cover your minimum payments,

20
00:00:36,548 --> 00:00:38,330
so we're assuming you can.

21
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:38,947
Let's go.

22
00:00:40,347 --> 00:00:40,732
First,

23
00:00:40,732 --> 00:00:44,063
why does debt feel like running up a down escalator?

24
00:00:44,323 --> 00:00:44,879
Interest.

25
00:00:44,879 --> 00:00:45,621
Every month,

26
00:00:45,621 --> 00:00:47,599
your lender charges a percentage

27
00:00:47,599 --> 00:00:48,959
of what you still owe.

28
00:00:49,219 --> 00:00:53,952
Say you owe $5,000 on a card at 24% APR,

29
00:00:53,952 --> 00:00:57,503
and you pay only $125 a month.

30
00:00:57,763 --> 00:01:00,163
It would take about eighty-two months,

31
00:01:00,163 --> 00:01:01,364
almost seven years,

32
00:01:01,364 --> 00:01:03,512
and cost roughly five thousand one

33
00:01:03,512 --> 00:01:05,660
hundred sixty dollars in interest.

34
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:07,619
More than the original balance.

35
00:01:09,019 --> 00:01:11,191
Let's watch interest in slow motion.

36
00:01:11,451 --> 00:01:14,968
$5,000 at 24% APR is 2% a month.

37
00:01:14,968 --> 00:01:20,354
That's $100 of interest in the first month alone.

38
00:01:20,614 --> 00:01:22,347
Your minimum payment is one

39
00:01:22,347 --> 00:01:24,143
hundred twenty-five dollars.

40
00:01:24,143 --> 00:01:27,479
So only twenty-five of it actually reduces the debt.

41
00:01:27,739 --> 00:01:29,658
That's why paying a little extra,

42
00:01:29,658 --> 00:01:31,054
aimed at the right debt,

43
00:01:31,054 --> 00:01:32,682
makes such a big difference.

44
00:01:34,082 --> 00:01:35,322
Here's our test case:

45
00:01:35,322 --> 00:01:36,030
three debts,

46
00:01:36,030 --> 00:01:38,745
totaling eight thousand three hundred dollars.

47
00:01:39,005 --> 00:01:39,878
A store card:

48
00:01:39,878 --> 00:01:42,565
eight hundred dollars at twelve percent.

49
00:01:42,565 --> 00:01:43,639
A personal loan:

50
00:01:43,639 --> 00:01:46,259
twenty-five hundred at fifteen percent.

51
00:01:46,259 --> 00:01:47,468
And a credit card:

52
00:01:47,468 --> 00:01:49,953
five thousand at twenty-four percent.

53
00:01:50,213 --> 00:01:52,316
The minimum payments add up to two

54
00:01:52,316 --> 00:01:54,233
hundred thirty dollars a month.

55
00:01:54,233 --> 00:01:56,274
We'll add an extra three hundred,

56
00:01:56,274 --> 00:01:58,439
for a total of five hundred thirty.

57
00:01:58,699 --> 00:02:01,098
Both methods follow the same rules.

58
00:02:01,098 --> 00:02:03,154
Pay the minimum on everything.

59
00:02:03,154 --> 00:02:06,102
Send every extra dollar to one target debt.

60
00:02:06,102 --> 00:02:07,747
And when a debt is gone,

61
00:02:07,747 --> 00:02:10,146
roll its payment into the next one.

62
00:02:11,546 --> 00:02:14,416
Here's the secret engine behind both methods:

63
00:02:14,416 --> 00:02:15,309
the roll-over.

64
00:02:15,569 --> 00:02:16,589
In the snowball,

65
00:02:16,589 --> 00:02:18,818
the first target gets three hundred

66
00:02:18,818 --> 00:02:20,601
twenty-five dollars a month.

67
00:02:20,601 --> 00:02:21,557
When it's gone,

68
00:02:21,557 --> 00:02:23,849
that payment plus the loan's minimum

69
00:02:23,849 --> 00:02:25,505
becomes four hundred five.

70
00:02:25,505 --> 00:02:27,544
Then the last debt gets the full

71
00:02:27,544 --> 00:02:28,817
five hundred thirty.

72
00:02:29,077 --> 00:02:32,128
The avalanche works the same way:

73
00:02:32,128 --> 00:02:34,624
$425, then $505, then $530.

74
00:02:34,884 --> 00:02:37,630
Payments snowball in size as debts disappear.

75
00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:39,034
That's the whole trick.

76
00:02:40,434 --> 00:02:42,537
In the left corner, the Debt Snowball.

77
00:02:42,797 --> 00:02:44,399
You list your debts from the

78
00:02:44,399 --> 00:02:46,230
smallest balance to the largest,

79
00:02:46,230 --> 00:02:47,776
ignoring the interest rate.

80
00:02:48,036 --> 00:02:48,768
In our test,

81
00:02:48,768 --> 00:02:50,722
that means the store card first,

82
00:02:50,722 --> 00:02:52,126
then the personal loan,

83
00:02:52,126 --> 00:02:53,408
then the credit card.

84
00:02:53,668 --> 00:02:55,103
Why do people love it?

85
00:02:55,103 --> 00:02:55,821
Quick wins.

86
00:02:55,821 --> 00:02:58,104
You knock out your first debt fast,

87
00:02:58,104 --> 00:02:59,995
and each win builds momentum,

88
00:02:59,995 --> 00:03:02,147
like a snowball rolling downhill.

89
00:03:03,547 --> 00:03:05,772
In the right corner, the Debt Avalanche.

90
00:03:06,032 --> 00:03:08,081
You list your debts from the highest

91
00:03:08,081 --> 00:03:09,675
interest rate to the lowest,

92
00:03:09,675 --> 00:03:10,870
ignoring the balance.

93
00:03:11,130 --> 00:03:11,896
In our test:

94
00:03:11,896 --> 00:03:14,767
the credit card at twenty-four percent first,

95
00:03:14,767 --> 00:03:16,363
then the loan at fifteen,

96
00:03:16,363 --> 00:03:18,277
then the store card at twelve.

97
00:03:18,537 --> 00:03:19,989
Why do people pick it?

98
00:03:19,989 --> 00:03:20,319
Math.

99
00:03:20,319 --> 00:03:22,892
Attacking the most expensive debt first

100
00:03:22,892 --> 00:03:25,136
means you pay less total interest.

101
00:03:32,936 --> 00:03:33,888
And they're off.

102
00:03:33,888 --> 00:03:35,912
Both fighters put in the same five

103
00:03:35,912 --> 00:03:37,995
hundred thirty dollars every month.

104
00:03:38,255 --> 00:03:41,358
The snowball clears the store card by month three,

105
00:03:41,358 --> 00:03:43,034
and the loan by month nine.

106
00:03:43,294 --> 00:03:45,550
But the avalanche is attacking the card

107
00:03:45,550 --> 00:03:47,055
with the highest interest,

108
00:03:47,055 --> 00:03:49,138
so its interest bill shrinks faster.

109
00:03:49,398 --> 00:03:50,514
By month fourteen,

110
00:03:50,514 --> 00:03:52,994
the avalanche has wiped out the biggest,

111
00:03:52,994 --> 00:03:53,924
costliest debt.

112
00:03:53,924 --> 00:03:54,544
Meanwhile,

113
00:03:54,544 --> 00:03:56,653
the snowball is still carrying it.

114
00:03:56,913 --> 00:03:58,285
And at the finish line...

115
00:03:59,685 --> 00:04:00,533
Final scores.

116
00:04:00,533 --> 00:04:03,860
Both methods leave you debt-free in month nineteen.

117
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:06,546
The snowball paid about fifteen hundred

118
00:04:06,546 --> 00:04:08,474
eighty-six dollars in interest.

119
00:04:08,474 --> 00:04:11,645
The avalanche paid about twelve hundred ninety-six.

120
00:04:11,905 --> 00:04:13,830
That's roughly two hundred ninety

121
00:04:13,830 --> 00:04:15,639
dollars saved by the avalanche.

122
00:04:15,899 --> 00:04:17,422
But look at the first win.

123
00:04:17,422 --> 00:04:20,292
The snowball cleared a whole debt in month three.

124
00:04:20,292 --> 00:04:21,874
The avalanche took fourteen

125
00:04:21,874 --> 00:04:23,397
months to clear its first.

126
00:04:23,657 --> 00:04:25,588
So the avalanche wins on money,

127
00:04:25,588 --> 00:04:28,827
and the snowball wins on speed to the first victory.

128
00:04:29,087 --> 00:04:32,087
And if your interest rates are all close together,

129
00:04:32,087 --> 00:04:33,227
the savings shrink,

130
00:04:33,227 --> 00:04:36,047
so the snowball's quick wins might matter more.

131
00:04:44,047 --> 00:04:45,548
So which one should you choose?

132
00:04:45,808 --> 00:04:48,789
Choose the avalanche if you're motivated by numbers,

133
00:04:48,789 --> 00:04:51,024
your interest rates are very different,

134
00:04:51,024 --> 00:04:53,718
and you can stay disciplined for the long haul.

135
00:04:53,978 --> 00:04:56,033
Choose the snowball if you need

136
00:04:56,033 --> 00:04:57,955
early wins to stay motivated,

137
00:04:57,955 --> 00:05:00,010
or if you've quit plans before.

138
00:05:00,270 --> 00:05:01,623
You can even mix them:

139
00:05:01,623 --> 00:05:04,021
start with a tiny debt for a quick win,

140
00:05:04,021 --> 00:05:05,988
then switch to the highest rate.

141
00:05:06,248 --> 00:05:09,125
The best method is the one you'll actually finish.

142
00:05:10,525 --> 00:05:12,416
A few ways to speed things up.

143
00:05:12,676 --> 00:05:15,487
Call your lenders and ask for a lower rate,

144
00:05:15,487 --> 00:05:17,578
or look into a balance transfer,

145
00:05:17,578 --> 00:05:20,847
but read the fees and promotional terms carefully.

146
00:05:21,107 --> 00:05:22,071
Send windfalls,

147
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:23,936
like tax refunds and bonuses,

148
00:05:23,936 --> 00:05:25,736
straight to the target debt.

149
00:05:25,996 --> 00:05:28,151
Pick up a temporary side income,

150
00:05:28,151 --> 00:05:30,440
and give every extra dollar a job.

151
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:32,206
And stop adding new debt.

152
00:05:32,206 --> 00:05:34,012
You can't empty a bathtub with

153
00:05:34,012 --> 00:05:35,337
the tap still running.

154
00:05:36,737 --> 00:05:38,949
Where does this fit in the fifty, thirty,

155
00:05:38,949 --> 00:05:39,704
twenty budget?

156
00:05:39,964 --> 00:05:42,989
Debt payoff lives in your twenty percent bucket,

157
00:05:42,989 --> 00:05:44,123
alongside savings.

158
00:05:44,383 --> 00:05:44,775
First,

159
00:05:44,775 --> 00:05:46,867
build the starter emergency fund

160
00:05:46,867 --> 00:05:48,174
from our last video,

161
00:05:48,174 --> 00:05:51,442
so one surprise doesn't push you back onto a card.

162
00:05:51,702 --> 00:05:54,017
Then point the rest at your target debt,

163
00:05:54,017 --> 00:05:56,042
and automate the payment on payday.

164
00:05:56,302 --> 00:05:57,870
And once the debt is gone,

165
00:05:57,870 --> 00:06:01,006
redirect that same payment to savings and investing.

166
00:06:01,006 --> 00:06:03,418
You already know how to live without it.

167
00:06:04,818 --> 00:06:06,434
Four mistakes to avoid.

168
00:06:06,694 --> 00:06:06,922
One:

169
00:06:06,922 --> 00:06:09,720
skipping the minimum payments on the other debts.

170
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:12,518
That triggers late fees and can hurt your credit.

171
00:06:12,778 --> 00:06:13,060
Two:

172
00:06:13,060 --> 00:06:15,388
having no starter emergency fund,

173
00:06:15,388 --> 00:06:18,280
so every surprise lands back on the card.

174
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:18,920
Three:

175
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:21,266
ignoring interest rates entirely when

176
00:06:21,266 --> 00:06:23,104
the gap between them is huge.

177
00:06:23,364 --> 00:06:23,930
And four:

178
00:06:23,930 --> 00:06:25,755
quitting after one bad month.

179
00:06:25,755 --> 00:06:27,956
A slip doesn't erase your progress.

180
00:06:29,356 --> 00:06:30,363
Let's recap.

181
00:06:30,623 --> 00:06:31,707
List your debts.

182
00:06:31,707 --> 00:06:34,281
Snowball means smallest balance first.

183
00:06:34,281 --> 00:06:36,653
Avalanche means highest rate first.

184
00:06:36,913 --> 00:06:38,756
Pay the minimum on everything,

185
00:06:38,756 --> 00:06:41,337
and send every extra dollar to the target.

186
00:06:41,597 --> 00:06:43,779
The avalanche saves more interest,

187
00:06:43,779 --> 00:06:45,962
the snowball delivers faster wins,

188
00:06:45,962 --> 00:06:48,658
and the best method is the one you finish.

189
00:06:48,918 --> 00:06:51,312
Next time, we decode your credit score:

190
00:06:51,312 --> 00:06:53,645
the five factors that actually matter.

191
00:06:53,905 --> 00:06:55,462
If this helped, subscribe,

192
00:06:55,462 --> 00:06:57,140
and tell me in the comments:

193
00:06:57,140 --> 00:06:58,458
snowball or avalanche?

194
00:06:58,718 --> 00:07:01,147
And if you learned something from this video,

195
00:07:01,147 --> 00:07:03,143
don't forget to watch our next video.

196
00:07:03,403 --> 00:07:05,918
This video is for education only and

197
00:07:05,918 --> 00:07:07,525
isn't financial advice.

198
00:07:07,525 --> 00:07:08,782
See you next time.

